From bdb7e7ebb5f0f3116b55a77d4d16b4fe18a85f4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:27:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] webxr: support WebGPU sessions with OpenXR on Linux

WebGPU cannot write to the DMA-BUF shared images that the OpenXR
backend uses on Linux (crbug.com/330385376), so the backend did not
offer the "webgpu" session feature.

On Linux, the projection layers of XRGPUBinding now draw into a shared
image of their own, in a new XRGPUCopySwapChain built on Linux only. At
the end of the frame it is copied, and scaled, into the layer's shared
image over the raster interface, as media layers do. Its width is
rounded down to a multiple of the layer count, as an odd width hits a
CHECK in XRGPUTextureArraySwapChain.

The Vulkan binding gives the shared images of WebGPU sessions raster
access and does not flip WebGPU frames, which are already top-down.

The copy can be removed once WebGPU can write to DMA-BUF shared images
on Linux.

Bug: 506004811
Change-Id: Ib3ec0aa75ea4917430c2ab40a9e2a5a45b5525c6
